# Build and run artifacts. Nothing generated is committed: a generated
# file in git is a file that can disagree with its generator, and the
# disagreement is invisible from either side.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
_site/
_work/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Reference material: consulted, cited, never redistributed.
#
# ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148:2018 is a paid standard. It was committed here and
# served from a public raw.githubusercontent.com URL while README.md said
# this repository does not redistribute it. The history has been rewritten
# to remove it; this keeps it from coming back.
#
# The files stay on disk because the work needs them. They are ignored
# rather than deleted, and tests/test_licensing.py asserts they are not
# tracked -- ignoring a file and it being absent from the index are
# different facts, and only the second one matters.
docs/Reference/
*.pdf
